  "title": "ERP paradigm of the Mobile BCI dataset",
  "description": "This dataset contains the event-related potential (ERP) paradigm portion of the Mobile BCI dataset. Scalp EEG from 24 healthy participants was recorded during a visual oddball (P300) task while they stood, walked, and ran. It supports research on brain-computer interfaces that work during locomotion, and it is distributed as a MOABB-derived BIDS dataset.",
  "methods_description": "Participants performed a visual oddball task with Target and NonTarget stimuli across 5 sessions each. EEG was recorded with a BrainAmp amplifier using 73 Ag/AgCl channels, referenced to FCz with ground at Fpz. Sampling rate was 100 Hz and 4 EOG auxiliary channels were included. Impedance was kept below 50 kOhm.",
